    "reason": "The English lemma 'uniform' (noun) primarily refers to a distinctive set of clothes worn by members of an organization (e.g., school uniform, police uniform). The Japanese expression '一定' (いってい) means 'constant,' 'definite,' or 'fixed amount/state.' While the *adjective* sense of English 'uniform' (meaning consistent or unchanging) aligns with '一定,' the *noun* sense of 'uniform' (clothing) does not. They are semantically distinct concepts.",
